{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>He will not grow dim.</b> The prophet hints concerning the clinging of spirit to body." "<b>And he will not race.</b> His body — it is from the doubled stems [hifil/piel pattern], from the root רצוץ [in the preceding verse], like ירון and שמח (Proverbs 29:6). And the meaning: he will not die. Or its meaning: a man will not compel him — like the meaning mentioned above — and this is the correct one." "<b>Until he sets justice in the land.</b> That his prophecy will be revealed. And this is the meaning of ולתורתו: the teaching of his prophecy, like לתורה ולתעודה (Isaiah 8:20), as I have explained."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:31.432042119Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}